## Akchour in brief

Akchour lies in **Talassemtane National Park**, a forested limestone massif in the Rif. From the village, trails climb the river gorges, between rock walls, natural pools and small cafés by the water.

The site is a classic day trip from Chefchaouen: you can get there by shared taxi, with a private driver or on an organised excursion.

## The two classic walks

From the entrance to the site, two routes are particularly popular:

- **the walk to the waterfalls**: the trail follows the river to a series of falls and pools. It includes rocky sections and a few climbs;
- **the walk to God's Bridge**: a natural rock arch spanning the river, impressive from below as well as from above.

Allow a good part of the day if you want to do both. Walking times vary a lot depending on your pace and your breaks: ask locally about trail conditions.

{% tip title="With a guide" %}
A local guide knows the trails, the tricky sections and the day's conditions. It is a real plus for a first visit or if you want to get off the busiest routes.
{% /tip %}

## Planning your day

- Good walking shoes that grip on wet rocks.
- A swimsuit and towel if you plan to swim (the water stays cool, even in summer).
- Water, a snack and sun protection.
- Cash for transport and the small cafés on site.

{% warning title="Weather and river" %}
After heavy rain, the river level can rise quickly and make some sections dangerous. Check the weather forecast and give up if in doubt.
{% /warning %}

## Hiking responsibly

The site is fragile and increasingly busy. Stay on marked trails, leave no rubbish, do not use soap in the river and respect the peace of the villages you pass through.

To include Chefchaouen in a longer trip, see our [two-week itinerary](/en/guides/two-week-morocco-itinerary).
